{
  "format": "srwb",
  "version": "1.0",
  "notebook": {
    "name": "Prolog Generates Lua: Compiler Demo",
    "cells": [
      {
        "type": "markdown",
        "code": "# Prolog Generates Lua\n\nThis workbook demonstrates UnifyWeaver compiling Prolog predicates into **Lua** code.\n\nThe workflow:\n1. Define Prolog predicates (facts + rules)\n2. UnifyWeaver detects the recursion pattern (transitive closure)\n3. The compiler generates idiomatic Lua with tables and BFS traversal\n4. Execute the generated Lua code in the Lua kernel\n\n**Requires:** Install the UnifyWeaver package first (Browse Packages).\n\n**Limitation:** Lua variables don't persist across cells. All generated code and queries run in a single cell.",
        "language": "markdown"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "code": "% Load UnifyWeaver compiler modules\n['../init'].\n:- use_module(unifyweaver(core/recursive_compiler)).",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "load_compiler"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "code": "% Define a family tree as Prolog facts\n:- dynamic parent/2, ancestor/2.\n\nparent(alice, bob).\nparent(bob, charlie).\nparent(bob, diana).\nparent(charlie, eve).\nparent(diana, frank).\n\n% Transitive closure: ancestor(X, Y) if X is an ancestor of Y\nancestor(X, Y) :- parent(X, Y).\nancestor(X, Y) :- parent(X, Z), ancestor(Z, Y).",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "family_tree"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "code": "% Compile ancestor/2 to Lua and append queries\ncompile_recursive(ancestor/2, [target(lua)], FullCode),\nformat(string(Seeds), 'add_fact(\"alice\", \"bob\")~nadd_fact(\"bob\", \"charlie\")~nadd_fact(\"bob\", \"diana\")~nadd_fact(\"charlie\", \"eve\")~nadd_fact(\"diana\", \"frank\")~n~nlocal results = find_all(\"alice\")~nprint(\"Descendants of alice: \" .. table.concat(results, \", \"))~nprint(\"alice -> eve: \" .. tostring(check(\"alice\", \"eve\")))~nprint(\"alice -> frank: \" .. tostring(check(\"alice\", \"frank\")))~n', []),\n(   sub_string(FullCode, Pos, _, _, \"-- Read parent\")\n->  sub_string(FullCode, 0, Pos, _, Core)\n;   Core = FullCode\n),\nformat(string(LuaCode), '~w~n~w', [Core, Seeds]),\nnb_write('lua_output', '.code', LuaCode).",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "compile_to_lua"
      },
      {
        "type": "markdown",
        "code": "## Generated Lua Code\n\nThe cell below contains the Lua code generated by UnifyWeaver.\nIt includes:\n- Table-based adjacency list (`rel`)\n- BFS graph traversal (`find_all`)\n- Reachability check (`check`)\n- Seeded family tree facts and queries\n\nRun it to compute ancestors!",
        "language": "markdown"
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "code": "-- This cell will be populated by the compiler.\n-- Run the 'compile_to_lua' cell above first.",
        "language": "lua",
        "name": "lua_output"
      }
    ]
  }
}
